            "text": "Usually because water is concentrated across those joints, from a downspout, roof drip or poor slope, or because the sand was never vibrated in and keeps settling. Loss at the edges points to missing edge restraint; loss into deepening dips points to a settling base. Each needs its own fix before refilling."
          }
