        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Keeping sand between pavers is mostly a matter of removing whatever is taking it. Normal settling is solved by refilling with angular sand and vibrating it in. Cleaning damage is solved by cleaning differently. Ants, runoff, spreading edges and a sinking base each need their own repair before any joint material will stay.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Once the installation is sound, polymeric sand or a joint-stabilising sealer extends the time between top-ups considerably. Inspect the joints and edges each spring, fix small losses while they are small, and the joints should stay full with very little effort.
          </p>
        </div>

